WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.050
Domain Name Server, DNS, is the next protocol
we are going to cover.

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:10.900
DNS runs on port 53, and the main function
of DNS is to map hostnames to IP addresses.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.500
Here is an example of a DNS table that maps
hostnames to IP addresses using A records,

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.650
hostname-to-IP address lookup records.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:23.500
While this DNS table just has entries for
devices on this network, there are 13 root

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:30.210
DNS servers worldwide that carry tables for
all web addresses and update them as web domains

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.140
are registered and assigned IP addresses.

